From d7617c6c3ace88fbe43083c0cbecd055e8e88169 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valery Petrov <valerypetrov@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 00:03:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the local shard's context copy alive for the insert that
 uses it

InterpreterInsertQuery keeps only a weak reference to its context, so the
context copy the background sink's local write was given died as the
temporary it was, and every distributed insert taking that path failed with
"Context has expired" (18 stateless tests). The copy is now a named local
that outlives the interpreter and its pipeline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016i1XnLC3KypZdaYYsfzqub
---
 src/Storages/Distributed/DistributedSink.cpp | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Storages/Distributed/DistributedSink.cpp b/src/Storages/Distributed/DistributedSink.cpp
index d15c1f5b5d1..dc779003a5b 100644
--- a/src/Storages/Distributed/DistributedSink.cpp
+++ b/src/Storages/Distributed/DistributedSink.cpp
@@ -868,10 +868,12 @@ void DistributedSink::writeToLocal(const Cluster::ShardInfo & shard_info, const
 
     try
     {
-        /// Its own copy, as a foreground job takes: the interpreter consumes insert_expected_table_engine on it.
+        /// Its own copy, as a foreground job takes: the interpreter consumes insert_expected_table_engine on it,
+        /// and it must outlive the interpreter, which keeps only a weak reference to its context.
+        auto local_context = Context::createCopy(context);
         InterpreterInsertQuery interp(
             query_ast,
-            Context::createCopy(context),
+            local_context,
             allow_materialized,
             /* no_squash= */ false,
             /* no_destination= */ false,
-- 
